            <div class="content-box">
              Every project is unique, but most of them follow a typical lifecycle, detailed below. If you only need a subset of these services, we are happy to help!
            </div>
            <div class="content-box highlight-box">
              <h1><b>Project Lifecycle</b></h1>
              <h4>Consultation</h4>
              <p><ul><li>We take ~1-hour to walk through your space, discuss your wants and needs, and take measurements and photos. We charge $150 for the time, but if you proceed with an installation that amount is credited towards your project.</li></ul></p>

              <h4>Design</h4>
              <p>
                <ul>
                  <li>We work with you to design a custom garden plan that will beautify your space while accounting for the specific conditions around your site.</li>
                  <li>Design scope typically includes a graphic, a written design document, a virtual review, plus one round of updates.</li>
                  <li>Design budget is set in advance, based on the size and complexity of the project.</li>
                </ul>
              </p>

              <h4>Installation</h4>
              <p><ul><li>We transform your garden design into reality. Our team handles the installation, which can happen all at once, or gradually over time depending on the scope of project and your budget.</li></ul></p>

              <!--h4>More Plants, Please!</h4>
              <p><ul><li>Whether it’s replacing cool season veggies with warm season, or upgrading your garden with additional beds/plantings, we’re happy to provide mid-season consultations and installations.</li></ul></p-->

              <h4>Site Management</h4>
              <p>
                <ul>
                  <li>Your garden is a living system that will require some amount of management to achieve the desired results, <i>especially</i> in the first few years. We provide that site management, typically once a month, and provide regular human-written updates.</li>
                  <li>We want our clients to feel empowered to take over site management once their garden is established. We provide a written garden management guide, as well as training and support to make that transition as easy as possible.</li>
                </ul>
              </p>
            </div>
